WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.781
route first completes shared-memory scans of the four category masks.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:17.375
In this final body excerpt, subtracting one from the token’s inclusive category prefix gives its stable rank. start sums earlier category counts; start plus rank gives a unique destination.

00:00:17.595 --> 00:00:23.355
All threads finish the scan barriers before reading prefix, and count precedes route in the same stream.

00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:26.591
Count categories.

00:00:26.811 --> 00:00:28.837
Build counts before routing starts.

00:00:29.057 --> 00:00:30.465
Find start and rank.

00:00:30.685 --> 00:00:33.373
Combine the category region and local order.

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:34.895
Write token ID.

00:00:35.115 --> 00:00:37.397
Give each token a unique stable slot.

00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:42.895
Device-memory phase results connect counting to placement.

00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:49.301
Atomics can count safely, but the order of atomic arrivals alone does not preserve token order.

00:00:49.521 --> 00:00:52.551
The explicit earlier-token rank supplies stability.
